From 939756318bfa396163e3f4bdc17eda4984bb448c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 22:22:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rewrite dashboard for the paid-only subscription model

The Academy no longer accepts free registrations, so every free-trial
concept is removed and the metrics are rebuilt around paying subscribers.

Removed (free-trial):
- conversion.ts, leads.ts, plan-acquisition.ts and the Funil/Leads pages,
  all built on the ActiveCampaign free-trial tag and the March/2026 program
  launch date that was hard-coded across backend and frontend
- the daily free-trial snapshot cron and its tag/list cache warm-up
- ActiveCampaign is now used only for the UTM fields, to attribute paid
  subscriptions to a marketing origin

Metric correctness:
- All subscription metrics now derive from one shared set of CTEs
  (lib/subscription-sql.ts). Overview composes the same functions the
  dedicated pages use, so the three divergent churn rates are gone.
- MRR history is measured point-in-time instead of reconstructed by a
  cumulative add/subtract, and the last point equals the live snapshot by
  construction. Exit dates no longer fall back to last_event_at, which is
  set to NOW() on every upsert and was dumping every end-dateless
  subscriber into the current month.
- Churn is divided by the base at the start of each month rather than by
  every row ever inserted, which drove the rate down as the table grew.
- Cancellations are bucketed by the event's own creation_date, not by when
  the webhook was received.
- PAST_DUE is normalised to DELAYED; the "Atrasados" KPI read a status
  nothing ever wrote, so it was permanently zero.
- The global period selector now reaches every metric; revenue ignored it.
- Billing interval is derived from the gap between charges when the payload
  provides it, instead of guessing from the plan name and defaulting to
  annual (a 12x MRR understatement when wrong).

New metrics: revenue churn, NRR, GRR, quick ratio, LTV, cohort retention
(logo and revenue), tenure distribution, voluntary vs. involuntary churn,
upcoming renewals, delinquency and recoverable MRR, and cash collected as
distinct from recognised MRR.

Charts use a fixed-order categorical palette validated for colour-vision
separation against the theme surface; the previous green/yellow pair
measured dE 4.2 under protanopia.

Verified against a scratch PostgreSQL instance seeded with active,
cancelled, undated, delinquent and price-less subscriptions plus malformed
webhook payloads: MRR, active counts and churn reconcile across all
endpoints, migrations apply cleanly to the pre-existing schema, and
degenerate windows do not divide by zero.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
